    <GaugingStation location="Felsted" name="Chelmer" number="37020">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">'Essex' profile gauging a rural, predominantly London Clay catchment with minor artificial influences.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Drowning commences at 0.6m, and varies in severity. Limit of reliable gauging is at 1.21m, higher flows estimated. Flood plain storage starts at 1.1m. No spillway. Hydraulic model used to derive rating for high flows. Reasonable fit to gaugings. One peak flow rating applied across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">'Essex' profile (modified Flat V Crump) weir with crest tapping.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in August 2021 (WINFAP Files v10).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Minimal abstractions, adjustments needed for STW and industrial effluent discharges.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Chalk in N, London Clay elsewhere, largely overlain with Boulder Clay and some glacial gravel. Rural, agricultural land use, predominantly arable land.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">EI</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="QMED within bank and well gauged." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Confident in performance of model derived rating for out of bank flows." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
